      ],
      "image": "assets/images/239506/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place pork chops in a large bowl and season all sides with adobo seasoning, sazón seasoning, garlic powder, black pepper, and salt; add 2 tablespoons Italian dressing and flip to coat.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/tKtMeulfb0ReF3cdNbFpaGtqMyo=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-239506-oven-baked-stuffed-pork-chops-ddmfs-step-2-3a2d781239464ac386e5cfc2d45b7ca8.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/239506/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bring 1 1/2 cups water and butter to a boil in a saucepan; add stuffing mix and cover.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/rhdDt11FHKERohKCW28z-ohv-_c=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-239506-oven-baked-stuffed-pork-chops-ddmfs-step-3-7aaf3a0e9f74439ba6053434e9701341.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/239506/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Remove saucepan from heat and set aside until stuffing absorbs water, about 5 minutes; fluff with a fork.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/EqemPrjJ33R8f00uBcrIwryCwL0=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-239506-oven-baked-stuffed-pork-chops-ddmfs-step-4-fb7ac6ae7e1d4a479ebae788cfd19f51.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/239506/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Remove pork chops from the bowl, reserving liquid and seasonings.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/tjPnaT5BBkW3QDUfTqoazTN6VSk=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-239506-oven-baked-stuffed-pork-chops-ddmfs-step-5-b29279f6d0294b6397ca61e4cfa9a83e.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/239506/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lay each pork chop flat on a cutting board and with a sharp knife held parallel to the board, cut a pocket into the pork, leaving three sides intact.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/-CCDtJWcoceViyFr1ksid0LNTnc=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-239506-oven-baked-stuffed-pork-chops-ddmfs-step-6-60e7be1985984abba0c7bd74422b82a6.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/239506/step_06.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Stuff each pork chop with stuffing and close the pocket using a toothpick.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/HEhFT4GGEMD_vcpWfRUmFbkmFWI=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-239506-oven-baked-stuffed-pork-chops-ddmfs-step-7-e0c0b57583aa4ccfb3902d2ef49f6f85.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/239506/step_07.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Arrange pork chops on a baking sheet. Mix remaining 1 tablespoon Italian dressing and 1 tablespoon water with reserved juices from pork chops; pour over pork chops.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/eEk-o_XxmkhTz4K0C3BByCAbFgg=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-239506-oven-baked-stuffed-pork-chops-ddmfs-step-8-1-1e0364a1002549039a203d96b67e484f.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/239506/step_08.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake in the preheated oven until pork chops are cooked through, 25 to 35 minutes. An instant-read thermometer inserted into the center should read at least 145 degrees F (63 degrees C).",
      "section": null,
